      "content": "#include <stdio.h>\n#include <stdlib.h>\n#include <assert.h>\n#include <string.h>\n\n/* qsort's comparator reads this shared, immutable input while bucket sorts run. */\nstatic char *sort_strings;\nstatic int sort_length;\n\ntypedef struct {\n\tlong int *data;\n\tlong int total;\n} bucket;\n\nstatic int compare_indices(const void *left, const void *right) {\n\tlong int left_index = *(const long int *)left;\n\tlong int right_index = *(const long int *)right;\n\treturn strcmp(sort_strings + left_index * sort_length,\n\t              sort_strings + right_index * sort_length);\n}\n\nlong int* bucket_sort(char *a, int length, long int size, int offset, int nbuckets) {\n\tlong int i;\n\tlong int start = 0;\n\tlong int *returns = NULL;\n\tlong int *counts = NULL;\n\tbucket *buckets = NULL;\n\n\tif (size <= 0)\n\t\treturn NULL;\n\n\treturns = (long int *)malloc(sizeof(long int) * size);\n\tcounts = (long int *)calloc((size_t)nbuckets, sizeof(long int));\n\tbuckets = (bucket *)malloc(sizeof(bucket) * (size_t)nbuckets);\n\n\t/* Count first, then assign disjoint, exactly sized ranges in returns. */\n\tfor (i = 0; i < size; i++) {\n\t\tint key = *(a + i * length) - offset;\n\t\tcounts[key]++;\n\t}\n\n\tfor (i = 0; i < nbuckets; i++) {\n\t\tbuckets[i].data = returns + start;\n\t\tbuckets[i].total = 0;\n\t\tstart += counts[i];\n\t}\n\n\t/* Fill the bucket ranges with indices into the original strings. */\n\tfor (i = 0; i < size; i++) {\n\t\tint key = *(a + i * length) - offset;\n\t\tbucket *b = &buckets[key];\n\t\tb->data[b->total++] = i;\n\t}\n\n\tsort_strings = a;\n\tsort_length = length;\n\tif (size >= 4096 && nbuckets > 1) {\n\t\t#pragma omp parallel for schedule(dynamic, 1) num_threads(4)\n\t\tfor (int j = 0; j < nbuckets; j++)\n\t\t\tqsort(buckets[j].data, (size_t)buckets[j].total,\n\t\t\t      sizeof(long int), compare_indices);\n\t} else {\n\t\tfor (i = 0; i < nbuckets; i++)\n\t\t\tqsort(buckets[i].data, (size_t)buckets[i].total,\n\t\t\t      sizeof(long int), compare_indices);\n\t}\n\n\tfree(counts);\n\tfree(buckets);\n\treturn returns;\n}\n\nvoid load(char **vString, long int *N, int *l, int *os, int *nb){\n   char *strings = NULL;\n   int      len,\n            offset,\n            nbucket;\n   long int n;\n\n   if (!fscanf(stdin, \"%d\", &len)) {\n      printf (\"ERROR len\\n\");\n      exit (1);\n   }\n\n   if (!fscanf(stdin, \"%ld\", &n)) {\n      printf (\"ERROR n\\n\");\n      exit (1);\n   }\n\n   if (!fscanf(stdin, \"%d\", &offset)) {\n      printf (\"ERROR offset\\n\");\n      exit (1);\n   }\n\n   if (!fscanf(stdin, \"%d\", &nbucket)) {\n      printf (\"ERROR nbucket\\n\");\n      exit (1);\n   }\n\n   nbucket = nbucket + 1;\n   len = len + 1;\n\n   strings = (char*) malloc(n * len);\n\n   for (int i = 0; i < n; i++){\n      if (!fscanf(stdin, \"%s\", strings + (i * len))) {\n      printf (\"ERROR %d\\n\",i);\n      exit (1);\n      }\n   }\n\n   *vString = strings;\n   *N = n;\n   *l = len;\n   *os = offset;\n   *nb = nbucket;\n}\n\nvoid print(char *strings, long int *index, long int n, int len){\n\n   for (int i = 0; i < n; i++){\n      printf(\"%d -> %s\\n\", i, strings + (index[i] * len));\n   }\n}\n\nvoid save(char *strings, long int *index, long int n, int len){\n   for (int i = 0; i < n; i++){\n      printf(\"%s\\n\", strings + (index[i] * len));\n   }\n}\n\nint main(int ac, char **av) {\n\n   char     *strings = NULL;\n   long int N        = 0;\n   long int *index   = NULL;\n   int      len      = 0,\n            save2File = 0,\n            offset,\n            nbuckets;\n\n   load(&strings, &N, &len, &offset, &nbuckets);\n\n   index = bucket_sort(strings, len, N, offset, nbuckets);\n\n   save(strings, index, N, len);\n\n   if (strings != NULL)\n      free(strings);\n\n   if (index != NULL)\n      free(index);\n\n   return EXIT_SUCCESS;\n}\n",
      "path": "src/bucketsort.c"
    }
  ],
  "hypothesis": "Replacing per-bucket insertion sort with qsort should remove quadratic behavior, while dynamically scheduling independent bucket sorts across at most four threads may improve large-input performance, especially when bucket sizes are uneven.",
  "notes": "The bucket ranges are counted and prefix-allocated before filling, so uneven distributions cannot overrun fixed-size per-bucket slices. The comparator preserves the existing strcmp ordering. No compilation or measurement was performed.",
  "sources_kept": [],
  "transformations": [
    "Count bucket populations and assign disjoint prefix-sum ranges in the index array before filling them.",
    "Replace insertion sort with qsort using the existing strcmp ordering on string indices.",
    "For inputs of at least 4096 elements, dynamically schedule independent bucket sorts with a four-thread cap; use a serial path for smaller inputs."
